# File: tests/blender/test_contract_validate.py, tests/blender/test_bake_tiling.py, tests/unit/test_texel_classify.py
# Generated from: specs/151-measure-texel-density-per-material-slot-and-exempt-trim-atlas-and-flat-colour-slots/requirements.md
Feature: Measure texel density per material slot and exempt trim-atlas and flat-colour slots

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Density is measured per material slot
    Given an environment piece whose mesh has several material slots
    When contract validation or the tiling bake checks texel density
    Then each slot's density comes from its own faces and is compared with the variant minimum on its own

  @SCN002
  Scenario: A mesh dominated by atlas and flat-colour faces passes when its tiling slots are dense enough
    Given a mesh with a passing tiling slot plus a declared trim-atlas slot and a flat-colour slot covering most of the surface
    When the density check runs
    Then no texel-density finding or error is produced for that mesh

  @SCN003
  Scenario: A failing slot is named
    Given a mesh with two tiling slots, one above and one below the minimum
    When the density check runs
    Then the finding and the bake error name the mesh and the failing slot's material with the measured px/m, minimum, and variant

  @SCN004
  Scenario: A flat-colour slot is exempt without any marking
    Given a slot whose faces all have UVs collapsed so its total UV area is effectively zero
    When the density check runs
    Then the slot is exempt as flat_colour

  @SCN005
  Scenario: A trim-atlas slot is exempt when the author declares it
    Given a material carrying the nmg_trim_atlas marker
    When the density check runs on a mesh using that material
    Then the slot is exempt regardless of its measured density

  @SCN006
  Scenario: An undeclared low-density slot still fails
    Given an unmarked slot with non-zero UV area below the minimum
    When the density check runs
    Then the slot fails and the remediation names raising density or declaring the material trim-atlas

  @SCN007
  Scenario: The report shows what was measured and what was exempt
    Given a density check has run on an environment piece
    When the validation report and the bake report are read
    Then each slot is listed with its Desktop and Mobile px/m or its exemption reason

  @SCN008
  Scenario: The declaration holds through finalize and on the Mobile variant
    Given an asset with a declared trim-atlas material
    When validate, bake, and variants run and the Mobile variant is validated
    Then the slot is exempt at every step, including on the baked material and its _Mobile counterpart

  @SCN009
  Scenario: Single-slot tiling meshes behave as before
    Given a mesh with one undeclared tiling slot
    When the density check runs
    Then it passes or fails at the same density as today with the same code and reason
